cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "PushT reproduction artifact: configuration, compute and sampling in a robot learning benchmark"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-07
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/JacksonHYD/vla-pusht-repro-artifact"
abstract: >-
  Code, per-episode evaluation results and source patches for a study of how much
  of a reported success rate in robot learning is attributable to policy
  configuration rather than to the method or the training budget. The artifact
  contains 200-episode paired evaluations of Diffusion Policy, ACT and SmolVLA on
  PushT, a 2x2 factorial over input cropping and backbone initialisation, eleven
  disjoint seed blocks measuring the evaluation noise floor, and patches against
  LeRobot v0.6.1 that make evaluation deterministic and per-episode results
  auditable. Model weights are archived separately.
authors:
  - family-names: Huang
    given-names: Yandong
    affiliation: "Beijing Information Science and Technology University"
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - benchmark evaluation
  - robot learning
  - imitation learning
  - variance decomposition
  - LeRobot
  - PushT